      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah you need to expand the node before and drop the index, this is how I would do it:\n\n```\n#define PWM_LED_0_0_PERIOD \\\n        DT_PWMS_PERIOD_BY_IDX(DT_INST_PHANDLE_BY_IDX(0, leds, 0), 0)\n\n#define PWM_LED_PERIOD_CHECK_ONE(node_id, prop, idx, ...) \\\n                BUILD_ASSERT(PWM_LED_0_0_PERIOD \u003d\u003d DT_PWMS_PERIOD_BY_IDX(node_id, idx), \\\n                      \"PWM LED period mismatch\");\n\n#define PWM_LEDS_CHECK_ONE(node_id, prop, idx)    \\\n        DT_FOREACH_PROP_ELEM_VARGS( \\\n                DT_PHANDLE_BY_IDX(node_id, prop, idx), pwms, PWM_LED_PERIOD_CHECK_ONE)\n\nDT_INST_FOREACH_PROP_ELEM(0, leds, PWM_LEDS_CHECK_ONE)\n```\n\nThough it only seems to work with the `_VARGS` variant for some reason, asked in the chat about it.",
